# Panel and harbor lane output. `run_codepolicy_harbor2_smr2_panel.py` writes
# lane working directories under `submissions/_panel/`, and every harbor lane
# writes a `rollout.json` carrying base64'd `~/.codex/auth.json` — Codex OAuth
# access AND refresh tokens — or a raw OPENAI_API_KEY (`adapters/harbor/scripts/_lib.sh:96-100`).
# Nothing expires, revokes, or deletes those files, so an untracked-but-not-ignored
# tree is one `git add -A` away from committing live credentials.
submissions/
rollout.json

# Codex run residue inside Harbor task bundles. A `codex exec` run with
# CODEX_HOME pointed at the bundle leaves `.codex/auth.json` behind — the same
# OAuth access and refresh tokens as above. One such credential was tracked in
# `adapters/harbor/bundles/code_policy_deo_hillclimb/` and is now revoked.
# `.cache/` is uv's archive tree from the same runs (~120MB of noise).
# These directories are run output, never bundle source: the Rhodes container
# pool packaging step tars a bundle wholesale, so anything left here ships to a
# container image and to S3.
.codex/
adapters/harbor/bundles/*/.cache/

# User-supplied proprietary game ROMs used only as local research oracles.
roms/

# Container-pool build staging. `pool/sync_vendor.sh` copies tracked engine
# trees here so the pool build context (the Dockerfile's own directory) has
# what it needs. The repo stays the source of truth; nothing is duplicated in git.
adapters/harbor/bundles/*/vendor/
